---
import '@/styles/global.css'
//import Soyjak from '../bookmarklets/soyjak.jsx'
//import Bookmarklet from '../components/Bookmarklet.astro'
import BookmarkletsWithDynamicUrls from '../components/bookmarklets.jsx'
import React from "react";

//glob bookmarklets folder and create array of names
const bookmarklets = ['soyjak', 'travolta', 'wonka'];
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<title>Astro</title>
	</head>
	<body>

		<h1 class="site-header"><span class="bookmarklet">Bookmarklet</span> <span class="meme">. Meme</span></h1>


		<section>
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Memes on any website</h2>
			<p>Now you can instantly react to any website’s design or content with the most iconic memes from the internet &mdash; right from your browser. With just a click from your bookmarks bar, you can drop the perfect reaction onto any page, whether it’s a confusing layout, a hilarious typo, or just something that deserves a meme-worthy response. No extensions, no hassle &mdash; just pure meme magic at your fingertips. </p>

		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6 ">How to use</h2>
			<p>Drag the bookmarklet button to your bookmarks bar. Once installed there you can click it from any website to add the meme over the website content.
				No installation, no extensions &mdash; just click and enjoy the reaction wherever you browse.</p>
		</section>

		<BookmarkletsWithDynamicUrls client:load />

	</body>
</html>
